WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:06.380
Before Groot was the gentle giant fans know
and love today, he was a monster.

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:07.380
Literally.

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:14.620
A 125-foot-tall, rampaging alien monster.

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:21.900
He stayed that way for 45 years, too, until
a sudden and unexpected turn transformed him

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:27.340
into a hero and paved the way for his membership
in the Guardians of the Galaxy.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:32.950
But during his five decades as a villain,
Groot caused quite a few problems — and,

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:36.950
honestly, that didn't really stop when he
joined the side of the angels.

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:40.690
As one of Marvel's monsters, Groot terrified
countless humans.

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:45.660
As a hero, he's always in danger of returning
to his villainous, uh, roots.

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:50.350
Here are just a few of the ways Groot has
terrorized the Marvel Universe.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:52.520
Overlord of timber

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:57.800
It's hard to believe, but back in the early
days of Marvel Comics, Groot was there right

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:02.940
from the beginning, even before The Fantastic
Four and The Incredible Hulk burst onto the

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:03.940
scene.

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:10.920
In 1960's Tales to Astonish #13, Stan Lee
and Jack Kirby published a story called "I

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:11.920
Challenged Groot!

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:17.650
The Monster from Planet X," in which a tree-like
beast crashes to Earth and attempts to kidnap

00:01:17.650 --> 00:01:22.830
the population of an entire city, hoping to
take his prisoners back to his home world

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:25.190
for nefarious experiments.

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:30.500
Normally, that wouldn't be a problem, but
superheroes didn't exist in the Marvel Universe

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:33.930
yet, so the village was officially boned.

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:36.980
That's because Groot isn't any normal alien.

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:42.630
He calls himself the "overlord of all the
timber in the galaxy" and gets stronger by

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:45.229
absorbing wood — no, really.

00:01:45.229 --> 00:01:51.909
And not only can Groot talk, but he towers
above the villagers like some kinda Woodzilla,

00:01:51.909 --> 00:01:53.840
destroying everything in his path.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:58.270
Groot brings the local forest to life and
begins rounding up his human subjects.

00:01:58.270 --> 00:02:04.940
Until, of course, one lowly scientist discovers
Groot's only weakness: termites.

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:10.330
As the insects chomp away at Groot's wooden
body, the creature withers and dies, leaving

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:12.990
Earth safe — for now.

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:14.450
Hulk smashed

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:20.480
The next time the Monster from Planet X appears
is in The Incredible Hulk Annual #5, in which

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:26.950
a recurring Marvel villain named Xemnu wants
to challenge the not-so-jolly green giant.

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:32.390
To do so , he resurrects Groot and a handful
of other old Marvel monsters — real cool

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:36.569
guys with names like Goom and The Electrifying
Blip.

00:02:36.569 --> 00:02:37.690
Y'know...winners!

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:43.250
After smashing his way through a fifth-dimensional
demon named Diablo and a mud monster called

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:44.349
Taboo, Groot takes his shot at the Bruce Banner's
bigger half.

00:02:44.349 --> 00:02:49.380
Groot's branches nearly choke the life out
of the Hulk, while planting his roots in the

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:54.110
ground makes Groot impervious to the Hulk's
gamma-powered punches.

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:59.010
Groot even whips out a wave of razor-sharp
thorns which seem all set to finish the Hulk

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:00.120
off for good.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:11.240
But all of these attacks make Hulk angry,
and you know how that goes.

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:16.770
Hulk blocks Groot's attacks with a stone,
which he proceeds to use to beat Groot into

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:18.330
a splintered stump.

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:21.880
But that wouldn't be the end of Groot — not
by a longshot.

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:22.880
Breakout

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:28.099
Groot is a hard guy to keep down — remember,
he's grown back from a twig more than once.

00:03:28.099 --> 00:03:33.680
In the 2005 one-shot Monsters on the Prowl,
readers learn that, at some point in the past,

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:38.849
the intergalactic super-nerd known as the
Collector rounded up all of Marvel's other

00:03:38.849 --> 00:03:42.910
classic monsters and locked them away in an
underground prison.

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:48.660
That's weird and vaguely sinister, but relatively
safe — at least until Mole Man busts the

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:52.800
prison wide open, freeing Groot and the whole
monster party.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:58.440
The army of monsters make their way from Canada
to New York, where they start stomping everything

00:03:58.440 --> 00:03:59.440
in sight.

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:04.810
Unfortunately for them, Marvel's "good" monsters
— the Thing, the Hulk, Giant-Man, and Beast

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:06.519
— are on the scene.

00:04:06.519 --> 00:04:11.410
Most of the monsters are easy pickings for
the experienced superheroes, but Groot puts

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:16.779
up a bit more of a fight, using his roots
to tangle up the Thing and Hulk.

00:04:16.779 --> 00:04:20.989
But ultimately, he's defeated by the team
of heroes and locked away — although, obviously,

00:04:20.989 --> 00:04:22.180
not for good.

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:25.300
Agent of S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:31.199
Groot's road to redemption begins in 2005's
Nick Fury's Howling Commandos mini-series,

00:04:31.199 --> 00:04:35.539
but not before the arbor-alien gets in a few
more licks.

00:04:35.539 --> 00:04:37.139
Under the leadership of S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:04:37.139 --> 00:04:42.050
agent Clay Quartermain, the Howling Commandos
are a band of monsters charged with hunting

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:45.290
and capturing other monsters — and that
includes Groot.

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:50.240
Quartermain and his team find Groot hiding
in a forest, but the S.H.I.E.L.D. agents plaster

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:54.759
Groot with sonic weapons, eventually capturing
the titanic tree.

00:04:54.759 --> 00:04:56.889
Groot's prison term is short-lived.

00:04:56.889 --> 00:05:02.240
The evil wizard Merlin sends an army of goblins
and other supernatural creatures to attack

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:04.169
the Howling Commandos' base.

00:05:04.169 --> 00:05:09.639
Quartermain opens the prison doors, freeing
Groot and the other prisoners, causing a stampede

00:05:09.639 --> 00:05:11.789
that turns the tide of the battle.

00:05:11.789 --> 00:05:15.580
While the other monsters flee, Groot stays
behind and helps the team.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:20.229
Traveling on Groot's back, the Howling Commandos
take the fight to Merlin's stronghold and

00:05:20.229 --> 00:05:26.270
put the wizard in his place — and give Groot
the redemption that he desperately craves.

00:05:26.270 --> 00:05:27.361
We are Groot

00:05:27.361 --> 00:05:32.860
Here's the big twist: the Groot who joined
the Guardians of the Galaxy might not be the

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:39.240
same one who terrorized Earth for 50 years,
since, apparently, everyone on Planet X is

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:40.409
named Groot.

00:05:40.409 --> 00:05:44.539
"GROOT, GROOT, GROOT, GROOT, GROOT!"

00:05:44.539 --> 00:05:50.900
That theory is confirmed in Guardians of the
Galaxy #14, which explores Groot's origins.

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:55.509
Before he left home, Groot lived peacefully
on Planet X, where a group of squirrel-like

00:05:55.509 --> 00:05:59.669
"maintenance mammals" keep the forests in
tip-top shape.

00:05:59.669 --> 00:06:05.099
One day, some young saplings decide to harass
one of the small critters, and that's when

00:06:05.099 --> 00:06:06.649
the trouble starts.

00:06:06.649 --> 00:06:11.409
Another young Groot — presumably, our Groot
— intervenes, saving the little creature's

00:06:11.409 --> 00:06:12.409
life.

00:06:12.409 --> 00:06:16.520
As the maintenance mammals thank the heroic
Groot for his interference, the other Groots

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:20.569
attack again, and that's when good-guy-Groot
tears them into pieces.

00:06:20.569 --> 00:06:24.659
As punishment, the ruling Groots exile him
from Planet X.

00:06:24.659 --> 00:06:30.210
Depending on how you look at it, Groot is
either a bully, a murderer, or both — so,

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:35.099
in a way, it doesn't matter if he's the same
Groot who debuted back in 1960.

00:06:35.099 --> 00:06:37.360
He's damaged goods no matter what.

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:39.069
Groot, destroyer of worlds

00:06:39.069 --> 00:06:43.729
Technically, this isn't something terrible
that Groot has done — it's something that

00:06:43.729 --> 00:06:50.009
he'll do in about 30 years, according to an
elaborate virtual-reality simulation.

00:06:50.009 --> 00:06:55.589
Rocket Raccoon #9 flashes forward to 2046,
and we see that Groot has returned to his

00:06:55.589 --> 00:06:58.999
original, colossal size and plows through
New York.

00:06:58.999 --> 00:07:03.550
He also plows through his longtime sparring
partner, the Hulk, who becomes a snack for

00:07:03.550 --> 00:07:05.110
the rampaging monster.

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:10.279
As Iron Man explains, the Avengers tried to
use Groot's regeneration powers to cure all

00:07:10.279 --> 00:07:11.279
diseases.

00:07:11.279 --> 00:07:17.069
But, as is often the case when it comes to
comic book science, the process backfired,

00:07:17.069 --> 00:07:20.020
turning Groot into a giant, mindless beast.

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:25.669
Tony Stark tracks Rocket down and tries to
enlist his help, but Rocket is old and bitter

00:07:25.669 --> 00:07:28.580
and wants nothing to do with any of Earth's
heroes.

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:34.039
Meanwhile, the rampaging Groot tears S.H.I.E.L.D.'s
helicarrier in half, sending Steve Rogers

00:07:34.039 --> 00:07:35.729
plummeting to his death.

00:07:35.729 --> 00:07:41.060
Iron Man soon follows, smooshed under Groot's
wooden fist.

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:48.059
Rocket finally arrives, half-drunk, and transforms
his ship into a giant mech to fight Groot,

00:07:48.059 --> 00:07:50.199
but it's no match for Groot's raw strength.

00:07:50.199 --> 00:07:54.059
He tears both the robot and his furry friend
to pieces.

00:07:54.059 --> 00:07:56.580
Still, it's not all in vain.

00:07:56.580 --> 00:08:02.179
Rocket's sacrifice snaps Groot back to his
senses and transforms the monster into a giant,

00:08:02.179 --> 00:08:07.499
life-giving tree, while Rocket goes down in
history as one of the world's most important

00:08:07.499 --> 00:08:08.499
heroes.

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:10.869
"I am groot!"

00:08:13.460 --> 00:08:15.099
"That's a really bad sign."

00:08:15.099 --> 00:08:16.099
Thanks for watching!

00:08:16.099 --> 00:08:18.689
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:08:18.689 --> 00:08:21.279
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

